OUT-OF-BOX CODING-THEORY EXTENSION

A sparse regenerative scaffold can be viewed as:

AN ERROR-CORRECTING CODE
OVER
RELATIONAL STRUCTURE.

This suggests a later comparator:

EXPANDER-LIKE SCAFFOLD.

Instead of storing:
arbitrary pair relations,

choose edges so the protected relational graph has:

- bounded degree;
- broad member coverage;
- multiple independent paths;
- balanced positive/negative constraints;
- no single landmark bottleneck.

Desired property:

SMALL STORAGE
+
PARTIAL EDGE LOSS

still permits:
GLOBAL STRUCTURAL RECONSTRUCTION.

This is not part of the H145 primary acceptance claim.

It is a preregistered exploratory extension.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE

A regenerative organism may need:

TWO STRUCTURAL TIMESCALES.

FAST:

mutable topology
optimized for:
current task structure.

SLOW:

sparse relational scaffold
optimized for:
recoverability.

The slow layer must not dictate:
what the current topology IS.

It only preserves:
enough constraints
to help rebuild
when the fast layer fails.

Thus:

THE REGENERATIVE SEED
SHOULD BE
STRUCTURALLY USEFUL

WITHOUT BECOMING:

STRUCTURALLY SOVEREIGN.

